{
  "_what": "Uber Base's real component contracts - name, component key, variant count and variant AXIS NAMES - harvested from the duplicated GALLERY, not the library.",
  "_why": "REFERENCES.md recorded Base's import as blocked on a library subscription and recorded a Gallery duplicate as useless because 'every component in the Gallery is remote: true, so duplicating it yields instances and no components'. Both halves of that were true and the conclusion drawn from them was wrong.",
  "_how": "getMainComponentAsync() on each of the 19,406 INSTANCES in the duplicated Gallery. An instance's main component is reachable even when it is remote and even when importComponentSetByKeyAsync refuses the very same component by key. 19,405 of 19,406 reached; 1 failed and is not explained.",
  "_the_correction": "A GALLERY DUPLICATE IS USELESS FOR IMPORTING AND COMPLETE FOR HARVESTING, and nothing here had distinguished those two uses. The recorded fix - subscribe the library - was for the wrong problem: reading a contract needs no subscription at all, only an instance. The blocker that has sat open since the programme began was never a blocker for this question.",
  "_and_the_counts_were_wrong": "The record said 92 sets and 3,211 variants. Measured through the instances: 126 SETS and 4,280 VARIANTS, plus 222 bare components (icons). The old figure counted what a top-level page walk could see; this counts what is actually referenced. Neither number is dishonest and only one is the contract.",
  "_third_confirmation_of_the_state_finding": "44 of 126 sets carry a State axis - Enabled/Active/Disabled/Pressed/Loading on Button, eleven values on Calendar Date. That is the THIRD independent confirmation, after my own 43 blocks and after Figma's Simple Design System, that a design system models STATE as a variant axis because a static drawing cannot hold a runtime value.",
  "measured_at": "2026-07-31T11:38:40Z",
  "source_file": "4mz4UC3nacI6UFEXnyzFJc",
  "source_note": "a duplicate of the Base Gallery community file, in the Principal's drafts. The LIBRARY is still not subscribed and its keys still do not import.",
  "instances_walked": 19406,
  "instances_reached": 19405,
  "instances_failed": 1,
  "sets": 126,
  "variants": 4280,
  "bare_components": 222,
  "sets_with_state_axis": 44,
  "_this_file_holds": "72 of the 126, the ones whose axes are a CONTRACT rather than a catalogue. Flags (217 country names), Avatar (40 portraits) and Lifestyle photos (38) are listed with their axis name and count because enumerating them would bury the real axes, and the eight _Path/_Input private elements and nine single-axis icon sets are omitted as not part of the public surface.",
